<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Atapuerca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1054">1054</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Atapuerca was fought on 1 September 1054 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgos">Burgos</a> between two sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sancho-iii-of-navarre">Sancho III of Navarre</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-leon">Ferdinand I of León</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> defeated and killed his elder brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garcia-sanchez-iii-of-pamplona">García Sánchez III of Pamplona</a>, who had been pressing claims to Castilian border lands. The battle shifted the balance of Christian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> towards Castile and León.</p></div>
